     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hello everybody!<div>Please I am a new user of the package ggplot and I really need your help please.</div><div>In fact, as you can see, when I performed this code : </div><div><br></div><div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\" face=\"georgia, serif\">load(file = &quot;U:/SAR125844_MODDE_Comparer/Code_R/donnee.RData&quot;)</font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\" face=\"georgia, serif\">z1 &lt;- donnee[,&quot;z&quot;]</font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\" face=\"georgia, serif\">lolim  &lt;- 0</font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\" face=\"georgia, serif\">bwdth1 &lt;- 40000</font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\" face=\"georgia, serif\">bwdth2 &lt;- 50000</font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\" face=\"georgia, serif\">bwdth3 &lt;- 60000</font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\" face=\"georgia, serif\">hilim  &lt;- 10^6</font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\" face=\"georgia, serif\">resolution &lt;- 32</font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\" face=\"georgia, serif\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\" face=\"georgia, serif\">subset.ST  = </font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\" face=\"georgia, serif\">  subset(donnee,</font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\" face=\"georgia, serif\">         (z == min(z1) | z == 1.65 |z == max(z1)))  </font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\" face=\"georgia, serif\">subset.ST$colcode &lt;-</font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\" face=\"georgia, serif\">  cut(subset.ST$level, breaks=c(lolim, bwdth1, bwdth2, bwdth3, hilim))</font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\" face=\"georgia, serif\">brk    &lt;-levels(subset.ST$colcode)</font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\" face=\"georgia, serif\">colors &lt;- c(&quot;green&quot;, &quot;yellow&quot;,&quot;orange&quot;, &quot;red&quot;)</font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\" face=\"georgia, serif\">c &lt;- ggplot(subset.ST, aes(x = x , y = y, z = level)) </font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\" face=\"georgia, serif\">c + facet_grid( ~ z)  + </font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\" face=\"georgia, serif\">  geom_tile(aes(fill = colcode), size = 2) +</font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\" face=\"georgia, serif\">  scale_x_continuous(name=&quot;x&quot;)       +</font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\" face=\"georgia, serif\">  scale_y_continuous(name=&quot;y&quot;)          + </font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\" face=\"georgia, serif\">  scale_fill_manual(name=&quot;Level&quot;,</font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\" face=\"georgia, serif\">                  breaks = brk, values = colors,</font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\" face=\"georgia, serif\">        labels=c(&quot;0 - 40&quot;, &quot;40 - 50&quot;, &quot;50 - 60&quot;, &quot;60 - 1000&quot;))</font></div></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\" face=\"georgia, serif\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"georgia, serif\">And I obtained this discontinuous graphic :</font></div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-1lDTMLGBlBs/VcR3lDwa9SI/AAAAAAAAAME/3EdGr8y93qk/s1600/Rplot.png\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-1lDTMLGBlBs/VcR3lDwa9SI/AAAAAAAAAME/3EdGr8y93qk/s1600/Rplot.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792368814453000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1O2TWzDQe721qriycNmKM_\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-1lDTMLGBlBs/VcR3lDwa9SI/AAAAAAAAAME/3EdGr8y93qk/s320/Rplot.png\" border=\"0\" width=\"320\" height=\"287\"></a></p><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"georgia, serif\">I tried to put  </font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255);font-family:georgia,serif\">c &lt;- ggplot(subset.ST, aes(x =as.factor( x) , y =as.factor( y), z = level))  </span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:georgia,serif\"><font color=\"#000000\">and it works however I really need to keep x and y continuous for other details.</font></span></div><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"georgia, seri